# {{ itsm_kb_vm_memory_modification_title }}

## Step 1 — Open ITSM service request

Open catalog **{{ itsm_vm_memory_modification_request_template_name }}** in itsm-app. Ask the user for `vm_name` and new `mem` (GiB). On submit, itsm-app returns `itsm_service_request_ref` (REQ-*) and `itsm_change_ref` (CHG-*). **User does not provide these refs** — take them from ITSM after submit.

## Step 2 — Launch AAP workflow

Launch **{{ aap_vm_memory_modification_pipeline_workflow }}** (org **{{ aap_vm_memory_modification_pipeline_organization }}**). Use step-1 refs plus user fields. Never ask the user for refs or invent them.

| Extra var | Req | Source |
|-----------|-----|--------|
| `itsm_change_ref` | yes | Step 1 (not user) |
| `itsm_service_request_ref` | no | Step 1 (not user) |
| `vm_name` | yes | User |
| `mem` | yes | User |

Example:
```
itsm_change_ref: CHG-13
itsm_service_request_ref: REQ-9
vm_name: server01
mem: 8
```

AAP: {{ demo_platform.aap.gateway_url }}

## Step 3 — Completion in chat

When the workflow finishes, a `[request.complete]` message appears as a **thread reply** under the `[request.submitted]` notification in **#operations**.
